The copy constructor is already a minimal member-wise copy with an empty body, so the only safe change is to keep the identical initialization order and empty body; any attempt to "optimize" it (e.g. memcpy) would be slower or risk behavioral differences.

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
    , profile(field.profile)
    , profileIndex(field.profileIndex)
    , type(field.type)
    , isFieldExpanded(field.isFieldExpanded)
{
}
```